{"summary":"Conversion to a function component, but the subscription effect lost the cleanup the class had — a live subscription leak with post-unmount state updates. The empty dependency array also introduces a stale-closure bug on `filter`. A new `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` for server-provided `description` has no sanitization or documented trust boundary, raising an XSS concern. Minor: relative import should use the `@/*` alias.","findings":[{"file":"src/components/MetricsPanel.jsx","startLine":18,"severity":"critical","category":"correctness","description":"The subscription `useEffect` calls `metricsClient.subscribe(channel, handleMetrics)` but never captures the returned subscription object and never returns a cleanup function. The original class component unsubscribed in `componentWillUnmount` via `this.subscription.unsubscribe()`. Every mount/unmount cycle now leaks a live subscription (and its `handleMetrics` closure), which keeps calling `setMetrics`/`setLastUpdated` after unmount — a real regression and a likely source of ghost state updates. Capture the return value and return `() => sub.unsubscribe()` from the effect.","suggestion":"useEffect(() => {
  const handleMetrics = ...;
  const sub = metricsClient.subscribe(channel, handleMetrics);
  return () => sub.unsubscribe();
}, [channel, filter]);"},{"file":"src/components/MetricsPanel.jsx","startLine":18,"severity":"major","category":"correctness","description":"The subscription effect depends on `channel` and `filter` but lists `[]` as deps. `filter` is captured in the `handleMetrics` closure at mount time, so if the `filter` prop changes later the visible metrics are still filtered against the original filter value (stale closure). The class version read `this.props.filter` at call time, so it always used the current filter. Either include `[channel, filter]` in the dependency array (and add the cleanup above so resubscription is safe) or read the latest filter via a ref.","suggestion":"}, [channel, filter]);"},{"file":"src/components/MetricsPanel.jsx","startLine":39,"severity":"major","category":"security","description":"`description` is rendered with `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` because it "arrives as rich text from the server." There is no sanitization shown, and the comment alone does not establish that the server output is trusted or constrained. If any user-influenced content can reach `description`, this is a stored XSS vector. Sanitize with a allowlisted sanitizer (e.g. DOMPurify) before injecting, or render structured data instead of raw HTML. If the server output is genuinely trusted and signed, document that invariant where the prop is produced.","suggestion":"<p ... dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: DOMPurify.sanitize(description) }} />"},{"file":"src/components/MetricsPanel.jsx","startLine":3,"severity":"minor","category":"style","description":"Per repo rules, imports under `src/*` should use the `@/*` alias. This file is in `src/components/` and imports `src/lib/metricsClient` via a relative path. Use `@/lib/metricsClient`.","suggestion":"import { metricsClient } from "@/lib/metricsClient";"}]}

